  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Reserve Bank of India, Database on Indian Economy (DBIE), read from our archived copy of it: the Section 42 return (report 689), food credit (1130), sectoral and industry-wise deployment of bank credit (the RBI's exports and monthly releases), money stock and reserve money (Data Query tables MSC_F, MSS_F, BMC_M, RMC_M and others), NPAs, capital adequacy and frauds (330, 1114, 329, 336, 1508), the spatial statements (1415, 1427, 1465, 1483), BSR-1 (941 to 963, 1134, 1555), NBFC credit, and bank ratios (332). CPI from MoSPI via the consumer prices guide. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage" set:html={T["prov-vintage"]} />.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>Amounts are converted from rupees or crore to ₹ lakh crore. Growth is computed from the published levels; for sectoral credit it uses the RBI's own printed year-ago figure wherever a release printed one, and equals the release. Shares and ratios are computed from levels. State totals add the RBI's bank-group and town-size rows. Nothing is estimated or filled; gaps are left empty.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions and breaks</h6>
        <p>Never joined across: the January 2019 sectoral reclassification; figures including and excluding the July 2023 HDFC merger; quarterly spatial statements with RRBs (to December 2022) and without (from March 2023); centres classed by the 2001 and 2011 censuses; Andhra Pradesh before and after Telangana, Jammu and Kashmir before and after Ladakh. Source defects corrected and disclosed in each file's notes.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Version 1.0, built October 2026 from RBI data to {PG.long}. Revised with each monthly sectoral credit release; banking health once a year.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fine">
      <span>Measure of India, money, credit and banks</span>
      <span>Vintage <span id="prov-vintage2" set:html={T["prov-vintage2"]} /></span>
      <span>Set in Newsreader and Libre Franklin</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

